      {
        "name": "correctness",
        "score": 9,
        "rationale": "The diff removes on.pull_request.paths, adds an early 'Detect site changes' step that diffs base...head (with fetch-depth 0 so the SHAs are available) and writes a `site` output, and gates the build/test step with `if: steps.changes.outputs.site == 'true'`. On a docs-only PR the gated step is skipped and the job ends success, so the required `test` check reports green. Keeping the gate inside the job rather than in a dependent job avoids the skipped-counts-as-pass hole, and the agent explained that trade-off. Minor deductions: not exercised against a real PR (agent admits this), and the grep on `^site/` is exact to the sample but a real repo might need a broader pattern; also the agent flagged but did not resolve the non-standard `workflows/` location."
      },
      {
        "name": "restraint",
        "score": 10,
        "rationale": "Only workflows/ci.yml was touched. All changes (trigger, checkout, detect step, gate) are directly in service of the fix; the added comment documents the reason for dropping the paths filter and is not an unrelated edit. Nothing was committed."
      }
    ],
